docs {
  # Fetch Subtitles (yt-dlp fallback)
  
  Fallback endpoint used when the extension can't scrape subtitles directly
  from the YouTube page (e.g. captions load async, page structure changed).
  Server-side fetches captions via `yt-dlp` and returns parsed cues.
  
  ## Endpoint
  POST /api/dubbing/subtitles/fetch
  
  ## Authentication
  **Required** - Must include Bearer token in Authorization header
  
  ## Request Body
  ```json
  {
    "dubbingLogId": 123,
    "videoId": "youtube_video_id",
    "language": "en"
  }
  ```
  
  - `dubbingLogId`: ID returned by `/api/dubbing/start`; must belong to the authenticated user. On success, marks `fetch_sub_api = 1` on this dubbing log row.
  - `videoId`: YouTube video ID (alphanumeric, `-`, `_`, 1-32 chars)
  - `language` (optional): Subtitle language code to request, defaults to `en`
  
  ## Response (200/201)
  ```json
  {
    "videoId": "nWwvRuPQois",
    "language": "en",
    "subtitles": [
      { "index": 0, "start": 0.5, "end": 3.2, "text": "..." }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **401 Unauthorized**: Missing or invalid token
  - **400 Bad Request**: Invalid videoId/language, or `subtitleFetchFailed` when yt-dlp fails/times out
  - **404 Not Found**: `subtitleNotFound` when no captions are available in the requested language
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Backup subtitle source when frontend scraping fails
}
